# L §5.4, §5.7, §5.14 (tally 2.1.2, issue #43, the S-close coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-03, confirmed by the user at
# G-SP1: "Confirm both"): a declared currency is a key of the prelude's `currencies`, so a leg of unit kind
# `currencies` carries money in it: in_cur moves 25.00 PLN from world into konto. tally 2.1.1's refcore refused it at
# load (LOAD-UNIT the amount of leg cash of in_cur is money PLN, not a unit of currencies), though its run took it.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind curs: event certain
  leg cash: currencies
input flag_amt: money PLN
input day: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move in_cur: curs
  on day
  at day
  leg cash from world to konto amount flag_amt

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), in_cur.cash.amount

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  flag_amt = 25.00 PLN
  day = 2026-02-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: (125.00 PLN, 25.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: in_cur
  cut 2026-06-30
